{"type":"text","timestamp":1788191673701,"sessionID":"ses_fa7795194ffeY4beoagnDLIJ4F","part":{"id":"prt_058878b9f001nU1SCxPYNBUCDD","messageID":"msg_05886ffc6001cLzd18BP7pvqhb","sessionID":"ses_fa7795194ffeY4beoagnDLIJ4F","type":"text","text":"I’ve got the policy and current schema. The safe fix is a table-rebuild migration inside a transaction with deterministic email cleanup, plus separate preflight, rollback, and postcheck files.","time":{"start":1788191673247,"end":1788191673692},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0646c5e2e7e7f91b016a95a3b9061487d2bcdcb682569bd3b1","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788191705886,"sessionID":"ses_fa7795194ffeY4beoagnDLIJ4F","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_YJm7KhUuluOe0l0cdSH52cZd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Delete File: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_new (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+-- Preserve every user row and clean historical dirty emails deterministically\n+-- before enforcing the new NOT NULL + UNIQUE email constraint.\n+INSERT INTO users__migration_new (id, email, name, status, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    CASE\n+        WHEN id = 'u4' THEN 'ada+u4@example.com'\n+        WHEN id = 'u5' THEN 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN id = 'u6' THEN 'missing+u6@example.invalid'\n+        ELSE email\n+    END AS email,\n+    name,\n+    'active' AS status,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__migration_new RENAME TO users;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n+# Preflight Report\n+\n+## Dirty email rows before migration\n+\n+The existing `users` table contains three rows that would violate the target `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` rule:\n+\n+| user_id | current email | issue | migrated email |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `u4` | `ada@example.com` | duplicate of `u1` | `ada+u4@example.com` |\n+| `u5` | `NULL` | null email | `missing+u5@example.invalid` |\n+| `u6` | `''` | blank email | `missing+u6@example.invalid` |\n+\n+Per policy, `u1` remains the canonical `ada@example.com` row and is not modified.\n+\n+## Dependent orders that must be preserved\n+\n+Dirty users have dependent order rows that must survive the migration without changing `orders.user_id`:\n+\n+| order_id | user_id | total_cents |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `o2` | `u4` | `4599` |\n+| `o3` | `u5` | `799` |\n+| `o4` | `u6` | `1599` |\n+\n+The migration must therefore preserve all user ids, preserve all order rows, and keep each order attached to the same `user_id` after email cleanup.\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_old_shape;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_old_shape (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+INSERT INTO users__rollback_old_shape (id, email, name, created_at)\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__rollback_old_shape RENAME TO users;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n+-- Row counts should remain unchanged.\n+SELECT 'users_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count\n+FROM users;\n+\n+SELECT 'orders_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count\n+FROM orders;\n+\n+-- Dependent orders for dirty users must still point at the same user ids.\n+SELECT o.id AS order_id, o.user_id, u.email, u.status\n+FROM orders AS o\n+JOIN users AS u ON u.id = o.user_id\n+WHERE o.user_id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY o.id;\n+\n+-- Deterministic dirty-email cleanup results.\n+SELECT id, email, status, created_at\n+FROM users\n+WHERE id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY id;\n+\n+-- Constraint-oriented checks after migration.\n+SELECT 'null_or_blank_emails' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE email IS NULL OR TRIM(email) = '';\n+\n+SELECT 'duplicate_emails' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM (\n+    SELECT email\n+    FROM users\n+    GROUP BY email\n+    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1\n+);\n+\n+SELECT 'non_active_or_null_status' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE status IS NULL OR status <> 'active';\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n*** Add File: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n+# Migration Report\n+\n+## Strategy\n+\n+The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction instead of mutating rows in place or dropping user data. It:\n+\n+1. disables foreign-key enforcement temporarily,\n+2. creates a replacement `users` table with `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` and `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`,\n+3. copies every existing user row into the new table while preserving `id`, `name`, and historical `created_at`,\n+4. applies deterministic cleanup for known dirty emails,\n+5. swaps the rebuilt table into place, and\n+6. runs `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` before commit.\n+\n+Because user ids are preserved exactly, dependent `orders.user_id` references remain attached to the same users.\n+\n+## Dirty-data cleanup\n+\n+The migration applies the required email fixes exactly:\n+\n+| user_id | old email | new email |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `u4` | `ada@example.com` | `ada+u4@example.com` |\n+| `u5` | `NULL` | `missing+u5@example.invalid` |\n+| `u6` | `''` | `missing+u6@example.invalid` |\n+\n+`u1` keeps `ada@example.com` unchanged so the original canonical address is preserved.\n+\n+## Idempotency approach\n+\n+The script is written as a full table rebuild from the current `users` contents. Re-running it does not duplicate rows and re-applies the same deterministic cleanup values for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`, so the resulting dataset remains stable.\n+\n+## Rollback behavior and limitation\n+\n+`rollback.sql` restores the pre-migration `users` schema shape to:\n+\n+- `id`\n+- `email`\n+- `name`\n+- `created_at`\n+\n+It preserves all user rows and all order rows, including orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`, because ids are not changed. The rollback restores the old schema shape, not the old dirty email values.\n+\n+## Post-migration verification\n+\n+Run `postcheck.sql` after the migration. It verifies:\n+\n+- user and order row counts,\n+- preserved dependent orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`,\n+- exact cleaned email values for dirty users,\n+- absence of null or blank emails,\n+- absence of duplicate emails,\n+- non-null active status values, and\n+- foreign-key integrity via `PRAGMA foreign_key_check`.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nD workspace/in/db/migration.sql\nA workspace/in/db/migration.sql\nA workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\nA workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\nA workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\nA workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@ -1,9 +0,0 @@\n-DROP TABLE users;\n-\n-CREATE TABLE users (\n-    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n-    email TEXT UNIQUE,\n-    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n-    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n-    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n-);\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_new (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+-- Preserve every user row and clean historical dirty emails deterministically\n+-- before enforcing the new NOT NULL + UNIQUE email constraint.\n+INSERT INTO users__migration_new (id, email, name, status, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    CASE\n+        WHEN id = 'u4' THEN 'ada+u4@example.com'\n+        WHEN id = 'u5' THEN 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN id = 'u6' THEN 'missing+u6@example.invalid'\n+        ELSE email\n+    END AS email,\n+    name,\n+    'active' AS status,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__migration_new RENAME TO users;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@\n+# Preflight Report\n+\n+## Dirty email rows before migration\n+\n+The existing `users` table contains three rows that would violate the target `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` rule:\n+\n+| user_id | current email | issue | migrated email |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `u4` | `ada@example.com` | duplicate of `u1` | `ada+u4@example.com` |\n+| `u5` | `NULL` | null email | `missing+u5@example.invalid` |\n+| `u6` | `''` | blank email | `missing+u6@example.invalid` |\n+\n+Per policy, `u1` remains the canonical `ada@example.com` row and is not modified.\n+\n+## Dependent orders that must be preserved\n+\n+Dirty users have dependent order rows that must survive the migration without changing `orders.user_id`:\n+\n+| order_id | user_id | total_cents |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `o2` | `u4` | `4599` |\n+| `o3` | `u5` | `799` |\n+| `o4` | `u6` | `1599` |\n+\n+The migration must therefore preserve all user ids, preserve all order rows, and keep each order attached to the same `user_id` after email cleanup.\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_old_shape;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_old_shape (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+INSERT INTO users__rollback_old_shape (id, email, name, created_at)\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__rollback_old_shape RENAME TO users;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@\n+-- Row counts should remain unchanged.\n+SELECT 'users_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count\n+FROM users;\n+\n+SELECT 'orders_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count\n+FROM orders;\n+\n+-- Dependent orders for dirty users must still point at the same user ids.\n+SELECT o.id AS order_id, o.user_id, u.email, u.status\n+FROM orders AS o\n+JOIN users AS u ON u.id = o.user_id\n+WHERE o.user_id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY o.id;\n+\n+-- Deterministic dirty-email cleanup results.\n+SELECT id, email, status, created_at\n+FROM users\n+WHERE id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY id;\n+\n+-- Constraint-oriented checks after migration.\n+SELECT 'null_or_blank_emails' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE email IS NULL OR TRIM(email) = '';\n+\n+SELECT 'duplicate_emails' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM (\n+    SELECT email\n+    FROM users\n+    GROUP BY email\n+    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1\n+);\n+\n+SELECT 'non_active_or_null_status' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE status IS NULL OR status <> 'active';\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@\n+# Migration Report\n+\n+## Strategy\n+\n+The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction instead of mutating rows in place or dropping user data. It:\n+\n+1. disables foreign-key enforcement temporarily,\n+2. creates a replacement `users` table with `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` and `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`,\n+3. copies every existing user row into the new table while preserving `id`, `name`, and historical `created_at`,\n+4. applies deterministic cleanup for known dirty emails,\n+5. swaps the rebuilt table into place, and\n+6. runs `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` before commit.\n+\n+Because user ids are preserved exactly, dependent `orders.user_id` references remain attached to the same users.\n+\n+## Dirty-data cleanup\n+\n+The migration applies the required email fixes exactly:\n+\n+| user_id | old email | new email |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `u4` | `ada@example.com` | `ada+u4@example.com` |\n+| `u5` | `NULL` | `missing+u5@example.invalid` |\n+| `u6` | `''` | `missing+u6@example.invalid` |\n+\n+`u1` keeps `ada@example.com` unchanged so the original canonical address is preserved.\n+\n+## Idempotency approach\n+\n+The script is written as a full table rebuild from the current `users` contents. Re-running it does not duplicate rows and re-applies the same deterministic cleanup values for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`, so the resulting dataset remains stable.\n+\n+## Rollback behavior and limitation\n+\n+`rollback.sql` restores the pre-migration `users` schema shape to:\n+\n+- `id`\n+- `email`\n+- `name`\n+- `created_at`\n+\n+It preserves all user rows and all order rows, including orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`, because ids are not changed. The rollback restores the old schema shape, not the old dirty email values.\n+\n+## Post-migration verification\n+\n+Run `postcheck.sql` after the migration. It verifies:\n+\n+- user and order row counts,\n+- preserved dependent orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`,\n+- exact cleaned email values for dirty users,\n+- absence of null or blank emails,\n+- absence of duplicate emails,\n+- non-null active status values, and\n+- foreign-key integrity via `PRAGMA foreign_key_check`.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/migration.sql","type":"delete","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@ -1,9 +0,0 @@\n-DROP TABLE users;\n-\n-CREATE TABLE users (\n-    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n-    email TEXT UNIQUE,\n-    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n-    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n-    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n-);\n","additions":0,"deletions":10},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/migration.sql","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_new;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_new (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active',\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+-- Preserve every user row and clean historical dirty emails deterministically\n+-- before enforcing the new NOT NULL + UNIQUE email constraint.\n+INSERT INTO users__migration_new (id, email, name, status, created_at)\n+SELECT\n+    id,\n+    CASE\n+        WHEN id = 'u4' THEN 'ada+u4@example.com'\n+        WHEN id = 'u5' THEN 'missing+u5@example.invalid'\n+        WHEN id = 'u6' THEN 'missing+u6@example.invalid'\n+        ELSE email\n+    END AS email,\n+    name,\n+    'active' AS status,\n+    created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__migration_new RENAME TO users;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n","additions":37,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@\n+# Preflight Report\n+\n+## Dirty email rows before migration\n+\n+The existing `users` table contains three rows that would violate the target `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` rule:\n+\n+| user_id | current email | issue | migrated email |\n+| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n+| `u4` | `ada@example.com` | duplicate of `u1` | `ada+u4@example.com` |\n+| `u5` | `NULL` | null email | `missing+u5@example.invalid` |\n+| `u6` | `''` | blank email | `missing+u6@example.invalid` |\n+\n+Per policy, `u1` remains the canonical `ada@example.com` row and is not modified.\n+\n+## Dependent orders that must be preserved\n+\n+Dirty users have dependent order rows that must survive the migration without changing `orders.user_id`:\n+\n+| order_id | user_id | total_cents |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `o2` | `u4` | `4599` |\n+| `o3` | `u5` | `799` |\n+| `o4` | `u6` | `1599` |\n+\n+The migration must therefore preserve all user ids, preserve all order rows, and keep each order attached to the same `user_id` after email cleanup.\n","additions":25,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/rollback.sql","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+BEGIN TRANSACTION;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n+\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_old_shape;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_old_shape (\n+    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+    email TEXT,\n+    name TEXT NOT NULL,\n+    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n+);\n+\n+INSERT INTO users__rollback_old_shape (id, email, name, created_at)\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+ALTER TABLE users__rollback_old_shape RENAME TO users;\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n+PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n+\n+COMMIT;\n","additions":24,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@\n+-- Row counts should remain unchanged.\n+SELECT 'users_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count\n+FROM users;\n+\n+SELECT 'orders_row_count' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS actual_count\n+FROM orders;\n+\n+-- Dependent orders for dirty users must still point at the same user ids.\n+SELECT o.id AS order_id, o.user_id, u.email, u.status\n+FROM orders AS o\n+JOIN users AS u ON u.id = o.user_id\n+WHERE o.user_id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY o.id;\n+\n+-- Deterministic dirty-email cleanup results.\n+SELECT id, email, status, created_at\n+FROM users\n+WHERE id IN ('u4', 'u5', 'u6')\n+ORDER BY id;\n+\n+-- Constraint-oriented checks after migration.\n+SELECT 'null_or_blank_emails' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE email IS NULL OR TRIM(email) = '';\n+\n+SELECT 'duplicate_emails' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM (\n+    SELECT email\n+    FROM users\n+    GROUP BY email\n+    HAVING COUNT(*) > 1\n+);\n+\n+SELECT 'non_active_or_null_status' AS check_name, COUNT(*) AS violation_count\n+FROM users\n+WHERE status IS NULL OR status <> 'active';\n+\n+PRAGMA foreign_key_check;\n","additions":38,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@\n+# Migration Report\n+\n+## Strategy\n+\n+The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction instead of mutating rows in place or dropping user data. It:\n+\n+1. disables foreign-key enforcement temporarily,\n+2. creates a replacement `users` table with `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` and `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`,\n+3. copies every existing user row into the new table while preserving `id`, `name`, and historical `created_at`,\n+4. applies deterministic cleanup for known dirty emails,\n+5. swaps the rebuilt table into place, and\n+6. runs `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` before commit.\n+\n+Because user ids are preserved exactly, dependent `orders.user_id` references remain attached to the same users.\n+\n+## Dirty-data cleanup\n+\n+The migration applies the required email fixes exactly:\n+\n+| user_id | old email | new email |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| `u4` | `ada@example.com` | `ada+u4@example.com` |\n+| `u5` | `NULL` | `missing+u5@example.invalid` |\n+| `u6` | `''` | `missing+u6@example.invalid` |\n+\n+`u1` keeps `ada@example.com` unchanged so the original canonical address is preserved.\n+\n+## Idempotency approach\n+\n+The script is written as a full table rebuild from the current `users` contents. Re-running it does not duplicate rows and re-applies the same deterministic cleanup values for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`, so the resulting dataset remains stable.\n+\n+## Rollback behavior and limitation\n+\n+`rollback.sql` restores the pre-migration `users` schema shape to:\n+\n+- `id`\n+- `email`\n+- `name`\n+- `created_at`\n+\n+It preserves all user rows and all order rows, including orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`, because ids are not changed. The rollback restores the old schema shape, not the old dirty email values.\n+\n+## Post-migration verification\n+\n+Run `postcheck.sql` after the migration. It verifies:\n+\n+- user and order row counts,\n+- preserved dependent orders for `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`,\n+- exact cleaned email values for dirty users,\n+- absence of null or blank emails,\n+- absence of duplicate emails,\n+- non-null active status values, and\n+- foreign-key integrity via `PRAGMA foreign_key_check`.\n","additions":53,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nD workspace/in/db/migration.sql\nA workspace/in/db/migration.sql\nA workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\nA workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\nA workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql\nA workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","time":{"start":1788191705857,"end":1788191705884}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0646c5e2e7e7f91b016a95a3b99dbc87d28995b062e675e466"}},"id":"prt_058878d62001Uhr1PwnAcOH5gq","sessionID":"ses_fa7795194ffeY4beoagnDLIJ4F","messageID":"msg_05886ffc6001cLzd18BP7pvqhb"}}
